{ia12}{offset110}{arial}
Radio Message from Bastogne
Operator: Sergeant Chief Barkod

from: Alex Kolman
1st Normo Army

to: {arialbld}{name}{arial}
2nd Normo Army





{offset0}Ah! {rank}, I'm so glad you could make it to Bastogne. You arrived just in time! An hour later would have been curtains for the tea, luckily we were able to save some cookies from the Tekton bombardments.{pause}

You won't have time to take off your shoes, I'm afraid {rank}.{pause}

The Psychos don't know what will be our next move, we must not give them time to think about it.{pause}


Flatland is a short day away by tank and only asks to be liberated from Tekton occupation. The Flatlanders preferred to nurture flowers over powerful armies, so were they helpless when the Psycho tanks came across their huge tulip fields.{pause}
The Tektons converted a great number of these from tulip to air fields, as launching bases for their bombing raids against Normland.{pause}
This windy country also used to have numerous windmills, the Tekton regime replaced these marvels of wood and canvas by "blockhauses" bristling with guns.{pause} This is the kind of architecture sponsored by Magnus von Tekton. We must fight against that.{pause}

The iron must be stricken while it's hot, we gonna tread on their wheels, pull the rug from under their treads, fling their tanks into the walls, kick them in the shins until they flutter a little white flag on their knees.{pause}

        
This operation is called {arialbld}"TULIP GARDEN":{arial}{pause}

We will jointly advance northwards on a front line going from {arialbld}Ostend{arial} in the west, where you will leave {name} with the 2nd army, to {arialbld}Maastrik{arial} in the south-east, where I'll be with the 1st army.{pause}

Our objectives are: {arialbld}the town of Nimeg,{arial} in the north-east, squatted by Karlo and his bomber fleet, the "Winged Wolves". And {arialbld}Haarlem,{arial} on the west coast, occupied by Tankred, where the harbour is the key to the entire Nordzee all the way to Legoland.{pause}{pause}










{center}{device33}










This mission will witness the christening of our new fighter: a super 800 hp dual motor, the Phoenix-38.{pause}


{offset150}{arialbld}Alex Kolman{arial}




{offset200}{signature1}{offset0}


{}
